{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the gateway models the clients offer: which",
    "id each surface lists, its display name and its token windows. It never",
    "says which upstream model answers - leg ORDER stays in",
    "configuration/omniroute/combos.json (and its LiteLLM mirror).",
    "",
    "List order = picker order on every surface.",
    "context: the 1M tier is 1000000 everywhere (operator ruling 2026-09-25);",
    "  the 128k tiers declare 131072, the conservative minimum across their",
    "  chains (docs/models.md: a display/compaction default, not a gate).",
    "output: the completion budget a surface declares for the model.",
    "reasoning_effort: optional per-model default, sent only by clients that",
    "  take one per model (Zed). OpenCode takes effort solely from #variants of",
    "  the provider catalog: never add a static variants/effort-alias block to",
    "  opencode.jsonc - it makes the whole provider unresolvable (measured).",
    "surfaces: gateway -> the surfaces that list the model through it.",
    "  gateways: omniroute (:20128 combos), litellm (:4000 fallback groups).",
    "  opencode  = opencode.jsonc providers.<gateway>.models (generated by",
    "              tools/sync-ide-models.py between // AUTOOS-MANAGED markers)",
    "              and the V1 user-config writers in lib/ (read at run time).",
    "  zed       = Zed language_models.openai_compatible.autoos-<gateway>",
    "              (both installers read this file at run time).",
    "  openhands = configuration/openhands/tier-profiles.json <gateway>-<id>",
    "              profiles: membership is checked, token windows are",
    "              mirrored there and into configuration/openhands/config.toml",
    "              by the same tool. The spec keeps its own push ORDER.",
    "Run python3 tools/sync-ide-models.py after editing; --check shows drift."
  ],
